+# FAA handwritten notes: a concrete limit on our text searches
+
+October 28, 2026 UTC. Existing B129 / PD01–PD04 and PD07; original-record work plan unchanged.
+
+**The held public FAA packet contains handwritten agent-note pages that our text searches and a fresh local OCR pass did not reliably read.** Four selected visible strings are absent from that OCR output even after removing spaces and punctuation. This is a demonstrated limitation of our search method, not evidence that an agency removed text. The pages offer specific underlying-note and policy-record leads. They do **not** supply the corrected Commission answer, delivery acknowledgment or signed administrative action/no-action decision.
+
+## Inputs and what was actually examined
+
+| Held public source | Physical pages | Selected low-text pages |
+|---|---:|---:|
+| [DOT-OIG interview release](https://www.governmentattic.org/42docs/DOToigFAA9-11interviews_2002-2006.pdf) | 4,380 | 77 |
+| [FAA/NEADS release](https://www.governmentattic.org/6docs/9-11FAA-NEADS-NORAD_2001-2005.pdf) | 257 | 13 |
+
+SOURCE-PINS.json preserves their existing URLs, original acquisition UTC, bytes and SHA-256. These are third-party-hosted released scans, not authenticated native notes, recordings or email systems. They were already held; **no new agency production or source PDF was acquired**.
+
+The selection rule was fewer than 100 non-whitespace characters in the existing hashed pypdf page extraction. It selected **90 pages**, not 90 missing documents or 90 unread substantive records. The threshold is a locator heuristic. A new visible-image pass rendered those pages in memory at scale2 and ran the existing local Tesseract with `--psm 3`. All90 selected OCR processes completed. No external OCR, installation, hidden-redaction recovery or source alteration occurred.
+
+Three 30-page contact sheets were visually inspected for triage. They show a mixture of handwritten notes, system screenshots, cover/divider sheets, maps, photographs and other reproduced material. Thumbnails do **not** support a claim of fully reading90pages. Four selected handwritten pages were then rendered and inspected individually in full. Five separate late-date keyword candidates were also inspected in full and identified as copies of printed CC-2006-085 pages2,3,9,10,12. Those copies do not constitute later management decisions or independent corroboration.
+
